(2) DOMAIN CONFINEMENT: every tight (worry-set) config has n∤v (construction side)
==============================================================================
  9 tight configs (n=4..8); with a multiple of n = 0  (0 => all construction-side, settled by THM-369)

==============================================================================
(3) GAUGE-BLINDNESS OF C': M is sign-invariant => C' truth is sign-invariant
==============================================================================
  explicit C' (n|v) instances — full 2^(n-1) sign-orbit, M constant?
    n=8 V=(8, 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7) (n|[8]): M-values across signs={'2/13'}; C'(M>1/n)=True; orbit-constant=True
    n=6 V=(6, 1, 2, 4, 5) (n|[6]): M-values across signs={'1/5'}; C'(M>1/n)=True; orbit-constant=True
    n=4 V=(4, 1, 2) (n|[4]): M-values across signs={'1/3'}; C'(M>1/n)=True; orbit-constant=True
  random sample: 1418 (V,sign) M-equality checks, 0 violations
  => M sign-invariant (incl. on C' instances): True

CONCLUSION: the sign group fixes M, hence fixes C''s truth; combined with (1) transversality and (2) domain confinement, the signed/2n-1 apparatus carries no DIRECT information about C' — the open core of LRC.
